WEBVTT

00:01:57.954 --> 00:02:01.163
where they are frontline
for minimum wage to help their families.

00:02:01.204 --> 00:02:03.788
They've attended
a makeshift funeral in the morning

00:02:03.829 --> 00:02:05.788
and a Google Meet in the afternoon.

00:02:05.788 --> 00:02:07.496
They are childcare providers,

00:02:07.538 --> 00:02:10.079
they are experiencing housing insecurity,

00:02:10.121 --> 00:02:12.496
they are scared, they are stressed,

00:02:12.496 --> 00:02:13.704
and they are children.

00:02:14.621 --> 00:02:17.829
When my son's teacher
asked a screen full of nine-year-olds

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:19.204
if everybody was OK,

00:02:19.913 --> 00:02:21.204
it almost broke me.

00:02:22.371 --> 00:02:23.496
"How are you?"

00:02:24.079 --> 00:02:25.371
"What do you need?"

00:02:25.829 --> 00:02:27.288
"Is your family safe?"

00:02:28.954 --> 00:02:31.746
School without school has been traumatic,